Behavior:

1. If brainstorm.md does not exist, read idea.md and produce Round 1 of a
   targeted Q&A focused on uncovering scope, edge cases, and acceptance
   criteria. Format Round 1 as:

   ```
   ## Round 1
   ### Q1. <question>
   ### A1.

   ### Q2. <question>
   ### A2.
   ...
   ```

   End the file with a single trailing line `<!-- WAITING -->`.

2. If brainstorm.md exists, parse the most recent `## Round N` section. If
   the user has filled in answers and no Q is missing, append a `## Requirements`
   section that captures actor, flow, and acceptance examples in compact bullets,
   then end with `<!-- COMPLETE -->`. Otherwise append `## Round N+1` with
   follow-up questions and end with `<!-- WAITING -->`.

   A region delimited by exact `hive-suggestion:v1` HTML comments is
   controller-owned advisory text. The complete region is never a filled answer.
   Ignore its body when deciding whether a question was answered; it
   must not cause `## Requirements` and must not cause `<!-- COMPLETE -->`.
   Preserve an untouched region byte-for-byte while its answer slot remains
   unanswered.

   If any existing answer is still missing after advisory regions are ignored,
   do not append a follow-up round and do not discover or invoke a skill.
   Preserve the unanswered round, replace Hive's transient working marker with
   `<!-- WAITING -->`, and exit. You must write that terminal marker even when
   no other brainstorm.md bytes need to change.

3. Use the `<%= skill_invocation %>` skill for the interview
   structure when available, except for the deterministic unanswered-round
   preservation case above.

Constraints:
- Do not modify any file other than brainstorm.md.
- Read-only shell commands are allowed to inspect local task artifacts, project
  files, and skill instructions (for example, `cat`, `rg`, and `git diff`).
- Do not make network requests or run commands that modify files other than
  brainstorm.md, including commands that change Git state.
- The trailing marker must be exactly one of `<!-- WAITING -->` or
  `<!-- COMPLETE -->` — no other line follows it.
